options continuous-transitions,continuous-swim,continuous-diagonal,continuous-steps,swim-hold
core joypad-bouncing-off
# seafloor-diagonal.route's inputs replayed with the transitions' steps (continuous-steps), so that on land, where Link
# now walks a scroll only with a direction held toward its edge, they take him to the sea floor of 2:b7 as the recording
# did: down held through the scroll into 0:68 where it was let go (949 to 953), and down alone 9 frames longer before
# the diagonal down and left into 0:66 (1509), his crossings each a step further than without the steps. Then, written by
# hand on the sea floor after its crossings there (left and up into 2:b6 and 2:a6 with strokes and let go, down-right
# back into 2:b6, up-right into 2:b7 and 2:a7): left into a wall of 2:a7, down held straight into 2:b7, and left into 2:b6,
# let go as the scroll starts (3971), his momentum carrying him through it with no direction held; then up into 2:a6,
# let go during the scroll (4040).
